From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: radv: trace every Orbis submit around the Titan Quest freeze window

The sparse submit trace reached #3000 but could miss an in-flight call at
#3001. Record every submit after #3000 through #4096, retaining the existing
first-16 and periodic samples outside that window. An unmatched enter then
identifies a submit blocked inside RADV; no new entry means the stall is above
the RADV queue boundary.

---
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c
index 087b578..f5c60d2 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_queue.c
@@ -2590,7 +2590,8 @@ radv_queue_submit(struct vk_queue *vqueue, struct vk_queue_submit *submission)
    static uint64_t orbis_submit_trace_count;
    const uint64_t orbis_submit_trace_n =
       __atomic_add_fetch(&orbis_submit_trace_count, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED);
-   const bool orbis_trace_submit = orbis_submit_trace_n <= 16 || !(orbis_submit_trace_n % 120);
+   const bool orbis_trace_submit = orbis_submit_trace_n <= 16 ||
+      (orbis_submit_trace_n >= 3001 && orbis_submit_trace_n <= 4096) || !(orbis_submit_trace_n % 120);

    if (orbis_trace_submit)
       mesa_logi("radv/orbis: queue submit enter #%" PRIu64 " command_buffers=%u waits=%u signals=%u",
